ents\u002Fclaude.svg","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.4.name":"OpenAI Codex","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.4.description":"CLI or VS Code extension","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.4.icon":null,"mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.5.name":"Windsurf","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.5.description":"Config file setup","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.5.icon":"assets\u002Ficons\u002Fmcp-clients\u002Fwindsurf.svg","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.6.name":"JetBrains IDEs","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.6.description":"AI Assistant settings","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.6.icon":null,"mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.7.name":"Gemini CLI","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.7.description":"CLI command setup","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.7.icon":null,"mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.8.name":"ChatGPT","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.8.description":"Custom connector (Dev mode)","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.8.icon":null,"mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.9.name":"Grok","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.9.description":"Bring Your Own MCP","mcpServer.supportedClients.blocks.9.icon":null,"mcpServer.supportedClients.cta":"Setup instructions →","mcpServer.ctaBlockConnect.headline":"Connect your AI assistant\nto 1inch — in seconds.","mcpServer.ctaBlockConnect.subtitle":"One-click setup for Cursor, VS Code, Claude, and 7+ other clients. Access nine MCP tools, then authorize protected swaps and Business API calls with API key or OAuth.","mcpServer.ctaBlockConnect.action":"View setup guide","mcpServer.ctaBlockBuild.headline":"Start building\nwith 1inch APIs.","mcpServer.ctaBlockBuild.subtitle":"Create an app, get API keys, and put Swap, Orderbook, Balance, and the rest of the suite into production—same stack you used through MCP.","mcpServer.ctaBlockBuild.actionSecondary":"Browse all APIs","pages.names.home":"DeFi Infra for Apps & Agents","pages.names.pricing":"Pricing","pages.names.enterprise":"Enterprise","pages.names.mcpServer":"AI Integration","pages.names.whatsNew":"What's new?","pages.names.ondoCaseStudy":"Ondo RWAs","whatsNew.page.title":"What's new?","whatsNew.page.subtitle":"Everything new across the 1inch APIs, SDKs, and developer tools.","whatsNew.detail.back":"← What's new","whatsNew.detail.share":"Share","whatsNew.meta.title":"What's new | 1inch Business","whatsNew.meta.description":"Everything new across the 1inch APIs, SDKs, and developer tools. Release notes and announcements for developers building on 1inch.","whatsNew.meta.schemaName":"What's new | 1inch Business","whatsNew.meta.schemaDescription":"Everything new across the 1inch APIs, SDKs, and developer tools. Release notes and announcements for developers building on 1inch.","whatsNew.card.learnMore":"Learn more","whatsNew.introducing-mcp-server.meta.title":"Introducing the 1inch MCP Server | 1inch Business","whatsNew.introducing-mcp-server.meta.description":"Agentic access to 1inch Business — connect Claude, Cursor, and 10+ AI clients to your docs, APIs, swaps, and debugging through the Model Context Protocol.","whatsNew.resolver-self-service-onboarding.meta.title":"Onboard as a resolver — now self-service | 1inch Business","whatsNew.resolver-self-service-onboarding.meta.description":"Register as a 1inch resolver in the Business portal — add Fusion, Fusion+, and limit-order contracts across chains and verify ownership on-chain, no manual process required.","whatsNew.robinhood-chain-support.meta.title":"1inch APIs are live on Robinhood Chain | 1inch Business","whatsNew.robinhood-chain-support.meta.description":"1inch now supports Robinhood Chain (chain ID 4663) — trade tokenized RWAs with 24\u002F5 availability, and the full suite of swap, data, and Web3 APIs.","whatsNew.introducing-observability.meta.title":"Introducing Observability | 1inch Business","whatsNew.introducing-observability.meta.description":"Monitor your 1inch API usage in the portal — requests, error rates, real request logs, on-chain swap volume, and quota usage across four new dashboard views.","whatsNew.mcp-agentic-swap-walletconnect.meta.title":"Agentic swaps with WalletConnect | 1inch Business","whatsNew.mcp-agentic-swap-walletconnect.meta.description":"The 1inch MCP Server can now quote and execute on-chain swaps — Classic, Fusion, and cross-chain — signed from your own wallet over WalletConnect.","whatsNew.mcp-search-docs-and-debug.meta.title":"Search docs and debug with the 1inch MCP Server | 1inch Business","whatsNew.mcp-search-docs-and-debug.meta.description":"The first 1inch MCP tools bring the developer portal into your AI client — search docs and API references, pull SDK examples, and debug your integration in place.","whatsNew.new-docs-api-playground.meta.title":"Interactive API Playground in the docs | 1inch Business","whatsNew.new-docs-api-playground.meta.description":"The 1inch docs now include an interactive API Playground — call any endpoint live, tweak parameters, and copy working code without leaving the docs.","caseStudies.ondo.meta.title":"Ondo RWAs | 1inch Business","caseStudies.ondo.meta.description":"How Ondo and 1inch power institutional RWA trading.","caseStudies.ondo.meta.schemaName":"Ondo RWAs","caseStudies.ondo.meta.schemaDescription":"How Ondo and 1inch power institutional RWA trading.","caseStudies.ondo.hero.headline":"How Ondo and 1inch power institutional RWA trading","caseStudies.ondo.hero.subtitle":"Real-world assets are becoming one of the largest opportunities in on-chain finance.","caseStudies.ondo.market.heading":"The market","caseStudies.ondo.market.bullets.opportunity":"Real-world assets are becoming one of the largest opportunities in on-chain finance.","caseStudies.ondo.market.bullets.sizePrefix":"The market is already worth ","caseStudies.ondo.market.bullets.sizeLink":"over $25 bln on-chain","caseStudies.ondo.market.bullets.sizeSuffix":", according to Dune, and is widely expected to grow even higher as tokenized treasuries, equities, funds and other financial products move onto blockchain rails.","caseStudies.ondo.market.bullets.institutions":"For institutions, this creates a clear infrastructure challenge: RWA products need more than issuance. They need efficient execution, broad distribution and reliable access to liquidity on-chain.","caseStudies.ondo.market.bullets.ondo1inch":"RWA tokenization platform Ondo Global Markets brings hundreds of tokenized stocks and ETFs on-chain. 1inch helps make those assets easier to access through efficient swap infrastructure, intent-based execution and a broad ecosystem of supported wallets, resolvers and liquidity providers.","caseStudies.ondo.bricks.heading":"The opportunity","caseStudies.ondo.bricks.p1":"RWAs are already seeing large-scale adoption.","caseStudies.ondo.bricks.p2":"Tokenized financial products are no longer only about proving that traditional assets can exist on-chain. The next phase is about making them usable:","caseStudies.ondo.bricks.tiles.access":"Easy to access","caseStudies.ondo.bricks.tiles.discover":"Easy to discover","caseStudies.ondo.bricks.tiles.trade":"Easy to trade","caseStudies.ondo.bricks.tiles.institutional":"Ready for institutional and AI-driven workflows","caseStudies.ondo.bricks.tiles.route":"Easy to route across chains and liquidity venues","caseStudies.ondo.intro.heading":"Ondo's mission is built around access: bringing financial assets on-chain via institutional-grade RWA infrastructure and giving users more ways to use those assets in DeFi.","caseStudies.ondo.intro.subheading":"But access only works if execution works.","caseStudies.ondo.problem.heading":"The problem","caseStudies.ondo.problem.paragraphs.p1":"RWA markets face a liquidity challenge.","caseStudies.ondo.problem.paragraphs.p2":"Primary issuance and redemption can be efficient when users interact directly with the issuer. But secondary-market liquidity is more complex. It involves buyers, sellers, market makers, resolvers, wallets, distributors and venues.","caseStudies.ondo.problem.paragraphs.p3":"For tokenized assets, the core challenge is not just liquidity. It is liquidity at an equivalent price to the underlying markets.","caseStudies.ondo.problem.paragraphs.p4":"Earlier models relied heavily on AMM pools. That created limits. Issuers or partners had to subsidize pools, or market makers had to commit balance sheet to assets that were still early in adoption. That model could work for small trades, but it was not enough for the scale of demand institutions and large on-chain users now bring to RWA markets.","caseStudies.ondo.problem.paragraphs.p5":"Institutional RWA trading needs a better market structure.","caseStudies.ondo.solution.heading":"The solution","caseStudies.ondo.solution.p1":"1inch provides swap infrastructure that aggregates liquidity sources and can be integrated by wallets, protocols and applications through a single layer.","caseStudies.ondo.solution.p2":"For RWA products, the most important part is intent-based execution.","caseStudies.ondo.solution.p3":"Instead of forcing the user or integrating app to manually find the best path, an intent lets the user define the outcome they want. Resolvers then compete to fulfill that outcome.","caseStudies.ondo.solution.p4":"This model is especially relevant for RWAs because execution may require several steps:","caseStudies.ondo.solution.items.sourcing":"sourcing liquidity from secondary markets;","caseStudies.ondo.solution.items.routing":"routing through stablecoins;","caseStudies.ondo.solution.items.participants":"interacting with authorized participants;","caseStudies.ondo.solution.items.mintRedeem":"supporting minting or redemption flows;","caseStudies.ondo.solution.items.price":"finding the best available price across venues.","caseStudies.ondo.solution.closing":"The user does not need to manage that complexity. The routing layer handles it.","caseStudies.ondo.why1inch.heading":"Why 1inch","caseStudies.ondo.why1inch.subheading":"1inch is a strong fit for RWA infrastructure because it combines three things institutions need:","caseStudies.ondo.why1inch.execution.heading":"Efficient execution","caseStudies.ondo.why1inch.execution.p1":"1inch intent-based swaps help abstract routing complexity. Users express what they want to achieve, and resolvers compete to deliver the result.","caseStudies.ondo.why1inch.execution.p2":"For RWA trading, this can help support more efficient access to secondary markets because different participants can compete to source the asset or route into the required settlement asset.","caseStudies.ondo.why1inch.access.heading":"Broad access","caseStudies.ondo.why1inch.access.p1":"1inch connects to a large ecosystem of wallets, protocols, liquidity sources and infrastructure partners. For issuers and RWA platforms, this matters because distribution is one of the hardest parts of bringing assets on-chain.","caseStudies.ondo.why1inch.access.p2":"Ondo's tokenized stocks benefit from being discoverable across the broader 1inch ecosystem, where wallets and other partners can access efficient swap infrastructure.","caseStudies.ondo.why1inch.scale.heading":"Infrastructure built for scale","caseStudies.ondo.why1inch.scale.p1":"The 1inch Swap API is designed for fast integration, multi-chain access and best-in-class execution. It gives developers a direct way to add swap functionality without building routing, liquidity discovery or execution logic from scratch.","caseStudies.ondo.why1inch.scale.p2":"For institutional teams, that means faster time to market. Integrators can plug into 1inch in minutes, not days, while relying on infrastructure built for real on-chain volume.","caseStudies.ondo.implementation.heading":"Implementation details","caseStudies.ondo.implementation.p1":"Ondo and 1inch work together through a broader execution ecosystem.","caseStudies.ondo.implementation.p2":"Ondo is the primary market issuer of its tokenized equities. Direct primary-market interactions require KYC-onboarded entities. 1inch plugs into the secondary-market layer, where ecosystem partners, resolvers, wallets and distributors help users access those assets through intent-based trading infrastructure.","caseStudies.ondo.flow.heading":"The flow can look like this:","caseStudies.ondo.flow.footer":"This model supports the same direction as Ondo Global Markets: making tokenized RWA access more efficient by connecting primary-market mechanics, secondary-market liquidity and user-facing distribution.","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.one.p0":"A user or app wants to access an","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.one.p1":" Ondo tokenized stock.","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.two.p0":"The user expresses","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.two.p1":" the desired trade ","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.two.p2":"through a supported wallet or interface.","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.three.p0":"1inch infrastructure routes ","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.three.p1":"that trade through available liquidity.","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.four.p0":"Resolvers and other market participants ","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.four.p1":"compete to fill the trade ","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.four.p2":"with the best available outcome.","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.five.p0":"The user receives access to the asset ","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.five.p1":"without manually managing ","caseStudies.ondo.flow.steps.five.p2":"each execution step.","caseStudies.ondo.proof.heading":"The proof","caseStudies.ondo.proof.subheading":"Since launch, 1inch infrastructure has routed substantial activity into Ondo assets:","caseStudies.ondo.proof.footnote":"* Data as of June 12, 2026. Source: Dune.","caseStudies.ondo.proof.footnoteLive":"* Live data, updated every 24 hours. Source: Dune.","caseStudies.ondo.proof.quote":"These figures cover every 1inch swap involving Ondo's tokenized real-world assets — USDY, OUSG and Ondo Stocks.","caseStudies.ondo.proof.stats.volume.value":"$5.5B","caseStudies.ondo.proof.stats.volume.label":"routed through 1inch-enabled flows","caseStudies.ondo.proof.stats.transactions.value":"2.8M","caseStudies.ondo.proof.stats.transactions.label":"transactions involving Ondo assets","caseStudies.ondo.proof.stats.users.value":"216K+","caseStudies.ondo.proof.stats.users.label":"users accessing Ondo assets","caseStudies.ondo.graph.heading":"Ondo activity on 1inch over time","caseStudies.ondo.graph.volume.heading":"Routed volume over time","caseStudies.ondo.graph.volume.p1":"Cumulative USD volume routed through 1inch in Ondo assets.","caseStudies.ondo.graph.volume.p2":"Totals are cumulative, so each month includes every trade before it.","caseStudies.ondo.graph.transactions.heading":"Transactions over time","caseStudies.ondo.graph.transactions.p1":"Cumulative number of 1inch transactions involving Ondo assets.","caseStudies.ondo.graph.transactions.p2":"A count that keeps climbing means usage is spread across many trades rather than a few large ones.","caseStudies.ondo.institutions.heading":"Why this matters for institutions","caseStudies.ondo.institutions.subheading":"Institutions need execution infrastructure before RWAs can scale.","caseStudies.ondo.institutions.p1":"Issuing tokenized assets is only one part of the market. The next phase requires:","caseStudies.ondo.institutions.items.access":"reliable access;","caseStudies.ondo.institutions.items.routing":"efficient routing;","caseStudies.ondo.institutions.items.pricing":"competitive pricing;","caseStudies.ondo.institutions.items.multiChain":"multi-chain support;","caseStudies.ondo.institutions.items.compliance":"compliance-aware distribution;","caseStudies.ondo.institutions.items.infrastructure":"infrastructure that can support wallets, platforms and AI agents.","caseStudies.ondo.institutions.closing":"1inch helps provide that layer.","caseStudies.ondo.institutions.p2":"As more financial products move on-chain, trading will become more automated, more intent-driven and more integrated into apps, wallets and institutional systems. In that environment, execution infrastructure becomes a core part of the RWA stack.","caseStudies.ondo.lookingAhead.heading":"Looking ahead","caseStudies.ondo.lookingAhead.body":"RWA adoption is moving from \"Can this asset be tokenized?\" to \"Can this asset be used?\"","caseStudies.ondo.lookingAhead.footer":"Ondo is helping bring institutional-grade financial products on-chain. 1inch helps make those products easier to access through efficient swap infrastructure and intent-based execution.","caseStudies.ondo.lookingAhead.closing":"Together, they point to the next phase of RWA markets: assets that are not only tokenized, but tradable, accessible and ready for institutional-scale on-chain finance.","caseStudies.ondo.bottomCta.title":"Build RWA trading flows with 1inch Swap API.","caseStudies.ondo.bottomCta.ctaLabel":"Swap API","askAi.launcher.open":"Open Ask 1inch AI support chat","askAi.launcher.title":"Ask 1inch AI","askAi.launcher.intro":"Hi! Ask me anything about 1inch Business. If you need a person, just say so and I’ll connect you with our support team.","askAi.launcher.placeholder":"Ask a question or type “contact support”","askAi.launcher.newConversation":"New conversation","askAi.launcher.handingOver":"Connecting you with our support team…","askAi.launcher.handoverPrefix":"Summary of my Ask 1inch AI conversation:","askAi.launcher.clearConversation":"Clear conversation","askAi.launcher.menu":"Chat options","askAi.launcher.expandWindow":"Expand window","askAi.launcher.collapseWindow":"Collapse window","askAi.launcher.talkToHuman":"Talk to human","gettingStarted.askAi.title":"Ask 1inch AI","gettingStarted.askAi.intro":"Describe what you are building and I’ll help to select the right products.","gettingStarted.askAi.placeholder":"I don’t know which product to choose","gettingStarted.askAi.thinking":"Thinking...","gettingStarted.askAi.errorUnavailable":"Error while loading the message","gettingStarted.askAi.errorQuota":"You’ve reached the Ask AI limit for today. Try again tomorrow or pick a product from the catalog.